# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Parking folders - never pushed, at any depth, in any app or project folder
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The 00__ prefix already means "not live" to the Python tools: the model sync
# and the DAS builder both skip folders whose name starts with it
# (SKIP_FOLDER_PREFIXES). This makes git agree with them, so one project folder
# can hold both the files a document uses and the ones kept only for context,
# without the second kind ever reaching GitHub Pages.
#   00__Archive   - superseded work kept for the record
#   00__Images    - pictures NOT used in the document, parked rather than deleted
# Matching is case-insensitive here (core.ignorecase is true), so 00__archive
# and 00__images are caught too. Already-tracked files are NOT untracked by
# these rules; they need git rm --cached.
**/00__Archive/
**/00__Archived/
**/00__Images/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Statement documents - the words are tracked, the pictures are not
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A statement folder under 10__StatementDocs holds its markdown, its generated
# HTML and the photography it is built from. The first two are small and belong
# in the repository. The third is not: RB05 alone holds 713 MB across reference
# images and content images, against a GitHub Pages deploy limit of 1 GB.
# The pictures are served from the CDN instead - the Statement Writer pushes
# every linked image to R2 and rewrites the HTML to its CDN URL - so nothing is
# lost by keeping them out of the repository.
# AN ALLOWLIST, not a list of picture extensions. A statement folder collects
# whatever the job needed - photographs, renders, a photogrammetry dataset, a
# zip somebody dropped in - and a list of the formats seen so far is a list
# that is one new format away from being wrong. So NOTHING under
# 10__StatementDocs is tracked except the three kinds of file that are the
# document itself. The first line excludes the folder; the second re-includes
# the directories, without which git cannot look inside to find the rest.
na-project-portal/**/10__StatementDocs/**
!na-project-portal/**/10__StatementDocs/**/
!na-project-portal/**/10__StatementDocs/**/*.md
!na-project-portal/**/10__StatementDocs/**/*.html
!na-project-portal/**/10__StatementDocs/**/*.json

# SHEET PICTURES (TrueVision Layout Editor, 54__Feature__SheetImages). The save
# files each picture a drawing shows into 05__Layout__DrawingDocs__Images/
# <document id>/ as a WebP cut to its print size, named <name>__<first ten hex
# digits of its SHA-256>.webp (or .jpg / .png), and the repository copy is the
# Pages fallback for the CDN. Nothing else there belongs in the repository: a
# render copied into the folder by hand is 10-20 MB of PNG (21-Sep-2026: 42 MB
# of them were), and 00__Archive holds pictures no drawing uses any more - the
# local safety net for an undo, never served. So, as for the statements, an
# ALLOWLIST, by the shape of the stored names: everything under the folder is
# excluded, the document folders are re-included so git can look inside them,
# the archive is excluded again, and only the stored pictures come back.
na-project-portal/**/05__Layout__DrawingDocs__Images/**
!na-project-portal/**/05__Layout__DrawingDocs__Images/*/
na-project-portal/**/05__Layout__DrawingDocs__Images/00__Archive/
!na-project-portal/**/05__Layout__DrawingDocs__Images/*/*__[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f].webp
!na-project-portal/**/05__Layout__DrawingDocs__Images/*/*__[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f].jpg
!na-project-portal/**/05__Layout__DrawingDocs__Images/*/*__[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f].png
